NETWORK USE (AGPL SECTION 13)

This program is normally run as a network service that other people talk to
through Discord. Section 13 is the reason this project is AGPL and not GPL: a
hosted bot is never "distributed" to its users, so a plain GPL would let a
closed source fork run in public with no obligations at all.

If you modify this program and let anyone else interact with it remotely, you
must offer those users the Corresponding Source of your modified version. The
/help command carries the source link so that offer is always one command
away. If you change the code, change SOURCE_URL in src/interactions.js to
point at your own repository. Leaving it pointed at this repository while
running modified code is a licence violation, not a shortcut.

Running an unmodified copy for your own community requires nothing from you.


